  "description": "With only a pinch of baking soda to help them brown, these waffles are leavened primarily by steam, so they're light and crisp, with a hint of tangy goodness.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: Maple syrup, for serving\n\nNotes: From size and depth to heat settings and materials (cast iron versus nonstick), waffle irons vary considerably from brand to brand; a small test waffle is a low-risk way to determine how the batter behaves on your machine.\nIn place of buttermilk, this recipe can be made with a 50/50 blend of plain, nonfat Greek yogurt and milk. You can also make this recipe without the vanilla bean, but the waffles won't be as aromatic.",
